7:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":"Atman is the spiritual life principle of the universe, especially when regarded as inherent in the real self of the individual. It is the eternal, unchanging, unmanifested core of conscious being, distinct from the mind, intellect, ego, and physical body. In Vedanta, recognizing the Atman is the key to liberation."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"italic border-l-2 border-primary/20 pl-6 py-2","children":"Understanding Atman is the core of Upanishadic teaching. The profound realization 'Aham Brahmasmi' (I am Brahman) points to the fundamental unity of the individual self (Atman) and the universal reality (Brahman)."}]]}]
